---SCREEN
=LINLIB/visi preferences setup

  Full explanation of this program accessible, see man vhset;
  Please, use arrow keys or .:TA... then .:NL... or .:SP... to make menu choice 

  On quit, profile will be untouched and settings are dropped.
  On exit, settings will be saved to profile, depending on write permission.

."profiles in order".                	
					1st found will patch compiled defaults;
    personal:    $VHSET/$TERM		no profile means no savings anyway
    system-wide: /etc/vhset/$TERM	

."How to create personal profile from bash:".

  export VHSET=~/.vhset; mkdir -p $VHSET; touch $VHSET/$TERM

=
There is one hidden page called with .'0 key. It allows to change
keypad activation key and labels for arrow keys which usually are never changed.
---END
